From bd3dd2ba024d6816bb8dd797b9cc190fda6b377e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: plotarmordev <299844489+plotarmordev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:04:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] nemotron: the CUDA Mamba scan steps kept and window
 rows in stages of 32

tf_nemo_scan loaded every step's inputs into shared memory at once, so a call took at most 32 kept and window rows
(windows of 16). It now loads and steps them 32 at a time; each step's arithmetic and order are unchanged, so a call of
up to 32 steps runs as before and longer calls give serial's bits. The glue test runs windows of 32 rows over 31 kept
ones (51 and 63 steps), alone and as a stream of a shared window.
